      "textEn": "361\n\nDogs—where; blessings—blessings, boon; Shruti-sukhah—sounds pleasing to the ear; like the mirage in the desert; where—where; this—this; body—body; Ashesh—infinite; pain—of disease; Viroha—place of origin; Nirvidite—\nbeing satisfied; not—not; but—but; people—common people; Yet—even so; thus—in this way; scholar—so-called\nphilosopher, scientist, and politician; Kama-analam—the flame of desire; honey—from the drops of honey;\nShamayan—controlling; Durapayah—very difficult to obtain..\n\nIn this physical world, every living being desires some kind of future happiness, which\nis like a mirage in the desert. Where is the water in the desert? In other words, in this\nphysical world, where is happiness? What is the value of this body, where does it hold? This is\nonly the source of various diseases. The so-called philosophers, scientists, and politicians know it very well,\nYet they desire momentary pleasure.\nIt is extremely difficult to attain happiness.\nBut because they cannot control their senses, they run after the so-called happiness of the material world\nand never reach the right conclusion. Meaning: It is a Bengali song, in which it is told that \"I built this house for happiness,\nBut unfortunately, it caught fire and now everything is burnt to ashes.\" This depicts the nature of material\nhappiness. Every person knows this, yet they want to hear or think of something that provides some kind of happiness. Unfortunately, with time, all his plans\nget destroyed. There have been many politicians who made plans for empire, superiority, and world domination,\nbut in chronological order, all their plans and empires—even the politicians themselves—were destroyed. Every person should take this lesson from Prahlad Maharaj that we are engaged in so-called momentary pleasure through physical practices for the sake of sensual enjoyment.\nWe\nmake all the plans again and again, which keep getting destroyed. Therefore, man should stop making such\nplans. Just as a person cannot extinguish a blazing fire by pouring ghee, similarly, no\nperson can be satisfied by making plans for their sensory gratification. This is the ignited fire, the world.\nIt is a great fire. In the forests, fire starts on its own; no one needs to try. We want to live happily in this world,\nbut it will never be possible, from this, in the burning fire of desires"
